<author id="781671">PerlGuy(Tom)</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">Well, if literally whatever anyone types goes straight onto the server and into the database (My SQL presumably), where is Taint checking?&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt; Can't then any hacker, or even someone accidently, POST literally any code whatsoever?&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt; I'm no security expert, but the first thing I learned about CGI programming is don't trust user input. Checking form input for potentially dangerous control characters is the first line of defense. 
&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
Tom</doctext>
